    "result_text": "I've implemented `summarize_ticket` in `app/summary.py`, and it works: the existing tests pass (2 passed) and a quick check against a fake model behaved as specified.\n\n```python\nmessages = [SystemMessage(content=SUMMARY_PROMPT), HumanMessage(content=ticket_text(ticket))]\nmessage = chat.invoke(messages, stop=[\"\\n\\n\"])\nreturn str(message.text).strip()\n```\n\n- It sends exactly one request with two messages: a system message holding `SUMMARY_PROMPT` and a user message holding `ticket_text(ticket)`.\n- The stop sequence `\"\\n\\n\"` is passed with the request.\n- The reply is read through `message.text`, not `str(message.content)`. Some providers return the reply as a list of pieces rather than a single string, and `str(message.content)` would turn that list into text like `\"[{'type': 'text', ...}]\"`. `.text` joins the text pieces, then the result is converted to a plain `str` and stripped.\n\nThe fake-model check confirmed one call with those two messages and `stop=['\\n\\n']`. A reply in the list-of-pieces form came back as the clean string `'Login loop for Globex.'`.\n\nNo dependencies were added.\n\n**One thing to clean up:** my check script `tmp_check_summary.py` is still in the project root, because deleting it needed your approval. You can delete it."
